# README criterion 5 (agent-exchange-2026-08 P12 G4): "An artifact that
# names a digest it does not carry is refused at `a2a validate`, locally,
# before any pull request." The readiness audit found the wiring from
# `a2a validate` to internal/validate's REF-017 check (checkPossession,
# possession.go) real by reading source, but no exec'd-binary run had ever
# asserted the refusal — this scenario is that run.
#
# AMENDED 2026-08-12 for ADR-011. REF-017 now refuses on a CONJUNCTION —
# an undeclared `sha256:` token AND a body that enumerates a file tree AND an
# envelope declaring no attachment at all — because a digest named in ordinary
# prose is a pin, not a claim to carry bytes, and refusing on it reddened a
# space's post-merge audit with no in-protocol repair (fb-20260812-e6d189).
# Both bodies therefore now carry the incident's own eight-file enumeration,
# which they had been simplified away from; the fixture is CLOSER to
# 03-bytes-note.md than it was, not further.
#
# The one-line-difference property survives and gets sharper: both artifacts
# now enumerate files and declare no attachment, so the file-tree leg and the
# no-attachment leg are held constant and the single differing line proves the
# DIGEST leg specifically. digest-not-carried.md is refused REF-017;
# digest-absent.md drops that one line and is valid (it warns POL-017, which is
# a warning and does not fail validation). Both frontmatter blocks are the internal/validate package's
# own possession_test.go incident reconstruction
# (docs/inbox/agent-exchange-review/03-bytes-note.md), adapted to this
# harness's fixture-space/axon/beta participants.
mkdir .a2a/staging
cp digest-not-carried.md .a2a/staging/digest-not-carried.md
! exec a2a validate --all
stdout 'REF-017'
rm .a2a/staging/digest-not-carried.md

cp digest-absent.md .a2a/staging/digest-absent.md
exec a2a validate --all
stdout '"valid": true'

-- digest-not-carried.md --
